From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Pettus <xof@thebuild.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:17:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/22] H6: Unicode fallbacks for CID fonts without ToUnicode

(a) `Type0Font::new` loaded the UCS2 CMap of the font's character
collection (Adobe-Japan1, -GB1, -CNS1, -Korea1) only when the font
program was not embedded. A CID of a known collection denotes the same
character whether or not the program is embedded, so the map is now
used whenever there is no `ToUnicode` map.

(b) For an embedded OpenType/TrueType program with no `ToUnicode` map
and no known collection (typically `Identity` ordering), map the code
to its glyph as drawing does (CID, then `/CIDToGIDMap`) and look the
glyph up in the program's `cmap`, inverted once per font on first use.
When several characters share a glyph, the lowest code point is used.
Substitute (non-embedded) fonts are excluded: their glyph IDs have no
relation to the PDF's CIDs.
